# ---------------------------------------------------------------- BANK-06, BANK-28, BANK OQ12
in_block(BANK, "BANK-06", "Two banks' terms read are BANK-33.",
         "Two banks' terms read are BANK-33. The Supervisor's liquidity directive counts a retail fixed deposit with more than 30 days left as fixed only if the depositor has no legal right to withdraw it within the 30-day period, or early withdrawal \"כרוכה בקנס משמעותי ששיעורו גדול מהותית מהפסד הריבית\"; if a bank lets depositors withdraw such deposits without that penalty, the whole category is treated as demand deposits, and any part withdrawable without it counts as on demand (directive 221 s.82, s.83, note 38). This shapes break pricing; the price itself is each bank's term (added 2026-10-26, open-question hunt).")
in_block(BANK, "BANK-06", "column \"אפשרות לשבירת פיקדון\" · checked 2026-10-25 · primary",
         f"column \"אפשרות לשבירת פיקדון\" · checked 2026-10-25 · primary; [{D221_T}]({D221}), p.20, s.82, s.83 and note 38 \"כרוכה בקנס משמעותי ששיעורו גדול מהותית מהפסד הריבית\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary")

in_block(BANK, "BANK-28", "Whether each monthly instalment has its own lock-up and exit points is not stated in any source read (open question 12).",
         "No general rule makes each instalment a separate sub-deposit with its own lock-up: the agreement must state the deposit schedule and amount limits (s.7(ב)(4)) and, for a deposit repayable before its final date, \"תנאי הפרעון המוקדם\" (s.7(ב)(5)), so the lock-up per instalment and the break price are each bank's plan terms (Bank Hapoalim's: BPN-10). Directive 221 counts as on demand any part of a fixed deposit withdrawable without a significant penalty (note 38 to s.82; BANK-06): it shapes break pricing but sets no price (open question 12, narrowed 2026-10-26, open-question hunt).")
in_block(BANK, "BANK-28", "p.5, s.7(ב)(4) · checked 2026-10-25 · primary",
         "p.5, s.7(ב)(4)-(5) \"תנאי הפרעון המוקדם\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary")
in_block(BANK, "BANK-28", "בנוסף על המפורטים בנספח א'\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary" if False else "נוספים על המפורטים בנספח א'\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary",
         f"נוספים על המפורטים בנספח א'\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; [{D221_T}]({D221}), p.20, note 38 to s.82 \"אם חלק מהפיקדון לזמן קצוב ניתן למשיכה מבלי לגרום לקנס כזה, רק אותו החלק ייחשב לפיקדון לפי דרישה\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary")

oq_append(BANK, 12, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** Narrowed: no general rule makes each instalment a separate sub-deposit. The disclosure rules require the agreement to state the deposit schedule and amount limits (s.7(ב)(4)) and the early-repayment terms (s.7(ב)(5)); a break goes on a form showing the nearest penalty-free date and the changed terms (s.10, BANK-06); directive 221 counts any part withdrawable without a significant penalty as on demand (note 38). So instalment lock-up and break pricing are each bank's plan terms (BANK-28, BPN-10). Still unknown: each other bank's plan agreement (instalment lock-up, the date exit points count from, break pricing).")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- TXI-04, TXI OQ2 (closed)
in_block(TXI, "TXI-04",
         "  - Prime-linked deposit (\"צמוד פריים\"): no source names it. On the statutory definition, the index is the CPI or an exchange rate, and the prime rate is neither. Read that way, such a deposit is \"not linked\" and taxed at 15%. This is my reading, not a published statement (open question 2).",
         "  - Prime-based deposit (\"צמוד פריים\", a variable rate): not linked to the index. The index is the CPI and, for a foreign-currency asset, the exchange rate (s.125ג(א); for withholding, s.88, through reg. 1 of the 2005 regulations), and a deposit counts as unlinked unless fully index-linked (guide 2025, \"אופן הצמדה\"), so all its interest is taxed at 15% (s.125ג(ג)(1)) and withheld at 15% (reg. 4, TXI-08). Directive 447 lists the rate type (\"משתנה/קבועה\") apart from the linkage (\"לא צמוד/ צמוד למדד המחירים לצרכן\"). No text names prime in words. Open question 2 closed 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt).")
in_block(TXI, "TXI-04", "(\"לרבות נכס שצמוד בחלקו לשיעור עליית המדד\") · checked 2026-10-25 · primary",
         f"(\"לרבות נכס שצמוד בחלקו לשיעור עליית המדד\"; for this definition the index is as defined in s.88) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{ORD_T}]({ORD}), p.146, s.88, definition מדד (\"על אף האמור, לענין נייר ערך בידי יחיד, הנקוב במטבע חוץ או שערכו צמוד למטבע חוץ, יראו את שער המטבע כמדד\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{D447_T}]({D447}), p.3, Annex A, columns \"סוג הצמדה\" and \"סוג ריבית\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary")
oq_replace(TXI, 2, "2. ~~**Prime-linked and other floating-rate deposits.**~~ Closed 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt): not linked; the statutory index is the CPI or, for a foreign-currency asset, the exchange rate (s.125ג(א), s.88), and the Tax Authority's guide counts a deposit as unlinked unless fully index-linked, so all its interest is taxed and withheld at 15% (TXI-04).")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- TXI-07, TXI OQ14
in_block(TXI, "TXI-07",
         "No rule specific to breaking a deposit early was found. Withholding attaches to interest actually paid, so a break that reduces the interest reduces the base, but no source says this in words (open question 14).",
         "No rule specific to a broken deposit exists in the texts read. The bank withholds on the interest it pays (reg. 4) and profits are taxed at withdrawal (guide 2025, sections 21-23), so on a break only the interest actually paid is taxed and withheld; what a break pays is the bank's term, shown on the break form (disclosure rules s.10, BANK-06). The Supervisor counts a retail fixed deposit as fixed for liquidity only if early withdrawal is barred or \"כרוכה בקנס משמעותי ששיעורו גדול מהותית מהפסד הריבית\" (directive 221 s.82), so a break can cost all the interest and part of the principal (BANK-33). Whether such a loss of principal has any tax effect is not stated anywhere read. Example (named, not the rule): Bank Hapoalim's fixed-rate deposit terms say it withholds when interest or linkage is credited to the deposit or the current account (\"ינכה הבנק מס הכנסה במקור\"), which bears on interest credited during a multi-year plan (open question 14, narrowed 2026-10-26, open-question hunt).")
in_block(TXI, "TXI-07", "p.42, sections 21-23 (\"מחויבים במס בעת המשיכה\") · checked 2026-10-25 · primary.",
         f"p.42, sections 21-23 (\"מחויבים במס בעת המשיכה\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{D151_T}]({D151}), p.6, s.10(א) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{D221_T}]({D221}), p.20, s.82 (\"כרוכה בקנס משמעותי ששיעורו גדול מהותית מהפסד הריבית\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [בנק הפועלים: פיקדון בריבית קבועה, תנאי עסקה]({HAP}), p.1 (\"ינכה הבנק מס הכנסה במקור\") · checked 2026-10-26 · institution.")
oq_append(TXI, 14, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** Narrowed: no source states a special rule for a broken deposit; the bank withholds on the interest it pays (reg. 4) and deposit profits are taxed at withdrawal (guide 2025, sections 21-23), so a break taxes only the interest paid at the break; what a break pays is the bank's term, shown on the break form (s.10), and directive 221 s.82 makes a fixed deposit count as fixed only if early withdrawal carries a penalty materially larger than the lost interest (TXI-07, BANK-06). Still unknown: a Tax Authority sentence on a broken deposit; whether a loss of principal from a break penalty has any tax effect; whether interest credited inside a multi-year plan is withheld at crediting (Bank Hapoalim's terms) or only at withdrawal (the guide's wording).")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- TXI-16, TXI OQ5
in_block(TXI, "TXI-16",
         "- Conditions / exceptions: The Minister may exclude kinds of investments or taxpayers from the rule (s.3(h1)). Whether any such order exists for traded government bonds, and how banks apply this to a private buyer between coupon dates, is open question 5. Do not compute the effect until it is closed.",
         "- Conditions / exceptions: The Minister may exclude kinds of investments or taxpayers from the rule (s.3(h1)); whether any such order exists for traded government bonds is not known. The withholding regulations have no accrued-interest provision: the payer withholds 15% (unlinked) or 25% (linked) from the interest it pays to an individual (reg. 5(א)), that is from the whole coupon paid to the holder on the payment date. At withholding a bank offsets the same year's securities losses under s.92 (2002 regulations, reg. 9(א)), and s.92(א)(4)(א) lets a securities loss be offset against interest on the same security; how that meets the s.3(ח)(1) bar for the accrued part, and how the price paid for accrued interest enters the cost, was not found (open question 5, narrowed 2026-10-26, open-question hunt). Example (named, not the rule): Bank Leumi's withholding page splits the withholding on interest or discount pro rata by accrual days across the legacy rate periods since the last payment (its note 3). Do not compute the effect on the price until it is closed.")
in_block(TXI, "TXI-16", "p.23, s.3(ח1) · checked 2026-10-25 · primary",
         f"p.23, s.3(ח1) · checked 2026-10-25 · primary. [{BTL05_T}]({BTL05}), p.2, reg. 5(א) (\"חייב המשלם ליחיד ריבית ינכה ממנה מס בשיעור של 25%\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{BTL02_T}]({BTL02}), p.2, reg. 9(א) (\"בחישוב רווח ההון לצורך ניכוי המס כאמור בתקנות אלה, יקזז החייב הפסד הון\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{ORD_T}]({ORD}), p.155, s.92(א)(4)(א)-(ב) (\"ואולם הפסד ההון יקוזז גם כנגד אלה\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [לאומי: ניכוי מס במקור בשוק ההון]({LEUMI}), note 3 to the withholding table · checked 2026-10-26 · institution")
oq_append(TXI, 5, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** Narrowed: for a buyer not in business s.3(ח)(1) treats the accrued interest as income with no exemption (other than one on the interest itself), credit, deduction or offset; the withholding regulations have no accrued-interest provision, so the payer withholds 15% or 25% from the whole coupon paid to whoever holds the bond (reg. 5(א)); s.92(א)(4) and reg. 9(א) of the 2002 regulations let a bank offset a same-year securities loss against interest on the same security (TXI-16). Still unknown: any order under s.3(ח1); a Tax Authority text on how the accrued interest paid at purchase enters the cost and whether the resulting loss may offset the coupon given s.3(ח)(1); the bank practice at a purchase between coupon dates.")

